
# Pigmee Fumo (ported from ae2lt)
itemGroup.pigtech.pigmee=Pigmee Tech
tile.pigmee_fumo.name=Pigmee Fumo
tile.creative_pigmee_fumo.name=Creative Pigmee Fumo
tooltip.pigtech.pigmee_fumo.1=You thought you were always one little pig,
tooltip.pigtech.pigmee_fumo.2=then around the corner was another just as slow and soft.
tooltip.pigtech.pigmee_fumo.3=You did not say much, but neither of you feared being alone anymore.
tooltip.pigtech.pigmee_fumo.4=May you meet the Pigmee meant for you -- MOAKIEE
tooltip.pigtech.creative_pigmee_fumo.1=Sometimes it misses an old board veiled in fine dust.
tooltip.pigtech.creative_pigmee_fumo.2=Craft it with one item to turn that item into a full stack.
tooltip.pigtech.creative_pigmee_fumo.3=The Pigmee remains, and every component of the item is preserved.
tooltip.pigtech.creative_pigmee_fumo.4=It is powerless against its own reflection.
tile.rainbow_pigmee_fumo.name=Rainbow Pigmee Fumo
tooltip.pigtech.rainbow_pigmee_fumo.1=It wears the sky after the rain.
tooltip.pigtech.rainbow_pigmee_fumo.2=Craft with one colorable item to cycle 16 colors; uncolored starts at white.
tooltip.pigtech.rainbow_pigmee_fumo.3=Place four identical items in a dye recipe layout to choose that color.
tooltip.pigtech.rainbow_pigmee_fumo.4=The Pigmee remains; it still makes dyes and Pigmee Building Blocks.
jei.pigtech.rainbow_pigmee.info=Pigmee once asked a shimmering sheep about the secret of its name. The sky answered with a rumble.
jei.pigtech.rainbow_pigmee.coloring=Craft with one colorable item to cycle white, orange, magenta, light blue, yellow, lime, pink, gray, light gray, cyan, purple, blue, brown, green, red and black. Uncolored items start at white. Replace the four Dye Bases in a dye recipe with four identical stackable items to color all four, keeping Rainbow Pigmee in the center. The Pigmee is reusable. Use single-item cycling for non-stackable items such as armor and shulker boxes. Mixed leather colors continue from the nearest Minecraft dye color. Items with all 16 color variants are supported; uncolored variants are identified from dye recipes with equal input/output quantities. Names, enchantments and stored contents are preserved.

